Purpose: The Google Password Manager enclave authenticator and the hybrid (phone, caBLE) transport are off: both relay through Google-run servers. The enclave is never offered; hybrid is off unless --enable-passkey-hybrid is given (until a settings toggle exists), so it is never used at idle or without an explicit choice.
Area: passkeys
Files: chrome/browser/webauthn/chrome_authenticator_request_delegate.cc (ConfigureDiscoveries: enclave condition, hybrid block), chrome/browser/webauthn/BUILD.gn (dep on //corvid/passkeys:google_features)
Rebase risk: medium (ConfigureDiscoveries changes between milestones)
Origin: original (written for Corvid; no third-party patch text reused); approach from the plan thread's note (do not flip webauthn_ui_enabled: it also hides the dialog)
Status: BUILT and run on 155.0.8059.39 (2026-10-18): the create dialog offers only "This device" and "USB security key"; passkey create and sign-in work. Not yet captured: a network capture during a passkey flow on a real site.

